course: dictionary
lesson: 14043
title: Manufactured: made by people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Manufactured is a form of the verb manufacture, and it can also describe things as an adjective. It means made by people, often in a factory using machines. The words around it give clues: «The toys were manufactured in a factory.» A factory is a building where machines make things, so manufactured means made there.
explain: Look for clues that show whether something is natural. «Plastic is a manufactured material, but wood comes from trees.» The word natural and the comparison with wood tell you that manufactured means made by people, not by nature. Try your meaning in the sentence: "made by people" fits, so you have it.
explain: The word can also mean made up to trick people. «The story was manufactured to get him into trouble.» Nobody found this story; someone invented it. Clues like story, evidence or trouble show this meaning, so check the whole sentence before you choose.
fact: Manufacture means to make goods, usually in large numbers in a factory.
fact: «Manufactured» means made in large numbers in a factory, using machines.
fact: Manufactured materials, such as plastic, glass and steel, are made by people. Natural materials, such as wood and wool, come from nature.
fact: «A factory manufactured 500 toys a day» means the factory made 500 toys every day.
fact: «Manufactured» can also mean made up or invented to trick people, as in «manufactured evidence».
exercise: «The factory manufactured 500 toys a day.» What does manufactured mean here? | Painted by hand | Broken and thrown away | *Made in large numbers in a factory | Sold cheaply in a shop
exercise: Which of these is a manufactured material? | *Plastic | Wool | Wood
exercise: «The evidence was manufactured to blame her.» What does manufactured suggest? | Shown on the news | *Made up to trick people | Found by a careful detective | Made from natural wood
test: «Steel is a manufactured material.» What does manufactured mean? | Found on the beach | Very old | *Made by people, not natural | Growing slowly in the ground
test: What does manufactures mean in «The company manufactures cars»? | Mends old cars | Drives cars very fast | Sells cars to shoppers | *Makes cars in a factory
exam: «The story was manufactured, so none of it was true.» What is the best meaning of manufactured here? | *Made up to trick people | Made of natural wool | Made in a factory with machines | Made into a film
